@startuml
title Service-token bootstrap (local PKCE helper) — v4

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
autonumber

actor Owner
participant "spotify-authorize.mjs\n(npm run spotify:authorize)" as Helper
participant "Loopback HTTP server\n127.0.0.1:port" as Loopback
participant "Spotify Accounts" as Accounts
participant "Spotify Web API" as Spotify
database ".dev.vars\n(ignored)" as DevVars
participant "npx wrangler\nsecret put" as Wrangler

== Setup and authorization request ==

Owner -> Helper: npm run spotify:authorize -- --local|--production
Helper -> DevVars: Read SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID, OWNER_SPOTIFY_ID\n(values are never printed)
Helper -> Helper: Generate PKCE verifier + state\n(cryptographically random, 43 chars)
Helper -> Helper: Derive S256 code challenge from the verifier
Helper -> Loopback: Listen on 127.0.0.1 only\n(registered redirect URI http://127.0.0.1:port/callback)
Helper --> Owner: Print authorize URL and try to open the browser\nscopes: user-library-read user-library-modify\nplaylist-read-private playlist-read-collaborative\nuser-read-private — exactly these, no playback scopes

Owner -> Accounts: Open URL, sign in as the owner, approve
Accounts --> Loopback: 302 http://127.0.0.1:port/callback?code&state

== Validation and exchange (no client secret) ==

Loopback -> Helper: Deliver the callback query
Helper -> Helper: Validate state with a constant-time compare\n(single use; reject mismatch, replay, or error params)
alt State mismatch, provider error, or missing code
  Helper --> Owner: Fail safely — nothing stored
else Callback is valid
  Helper -> Accounts: POST /api/token\ngrant_type=authorization_code\ncode + code_verifier + client_id\n(**no client_secret**)
  Accounts --> Helper: refresh_token + access_token + granted scope

  Helper -> Helper: Verify granted scopes include all five service scopes
  Helper -> Spotify: GET /v1/me (Bearer access_token)
  Spotify --> Helper: Account identity

  Helper --> Owner: Show the authenticated account\n(display name, immutable account_id, user id)
  alt account_id is absent or not OWNER_SPOTIFY_ID
    Helper --> Owner: Fail safely — nothing stored
  else Configured owner (after --yes or a y/N prompt)
    opt --local
      Helper -> DevVars: Atomically rewrite only the\nSPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN line\n(other entries preserved, mode 0600)
      Helper --> Owner: Report success — the token value is never printed
    end
    opt --production
      Helper -> Wrangler: spawn("npx", ["wrangler", "secret", "put",\n"SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN"])\nargv array, no shell
      Helper -> Wrangler: Write the token to child stdin only
      Wrangler --> Helper: Exit code
      Helper --> Owner: Report success — the token value is never printed
    end
  end
end

note over Helper,Wrangler #FFF2CC
  The refresh token never appears in the terminal, in argv,
  or in a shell command line. The browser identity token
  (flow 01) is a different token and is never written here.
end note

@enduml
